# This project supports two ways of getting a dev shell:
#
# 1. Plain `nix develop` (recommended for most people)
#    - No `devenv` CLI required.
#    - Just Nix + direnv (with nix-direnv) is enough.
#
# 2. `devenv shell` (for people who want the extra devenv features:
#    processes, `devenv up`, tasks, git-hooks, etc.)
#
# By default we activate the plain dev shell so that *anyone*
# can contribute without installing extra tools.

use flake

# If you prefer the devenv-powered shell (and have the CLI), you can
# switch by commenting the line above and uncommenting this one:
#
# use devenv
